Viśvāmitra abandons south and performs fierce austerities at Puṣkara --- Ambarīṣa begins sacrifice and Indra steals sacrificial animal --- Priest orders human victim as expiation before rite lapses --- Ambarīṣa searches kingdoms offering herds for victim --- Ambarīṣa finds R̥cīka with wife and sons at Bhr̥gutuṅga --- R̥cīka refuses eldest and wife shields youngest --- Middle son Śunaḥśēpa volunteers for sale --- Ambarīṣa buys Śunaḥśēpa for hundred thousand cows and departs by chariot